WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.270
"Sukunabikona Foods, supplement factory"

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.780
"Underground receiving bay"

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:10.150
This is Assault Team 1.
Commencing the operation.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:36.940
Move in!

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.960
Damn those Antiskill!

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.670
How did they know about this place?

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:19.090
These fools can't
comprehend our sublime ideas!

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.530
All squads are making entry
through the freight elevator.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.250
They are now engaging DA
at Transfer Station 1.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.440
DA troops appear to be resisting them,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.570
using shipping containers
and vehicles as barricades.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.240
What's their status?

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.330
They seem to have established their
momentum in the first ten seconds.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:42.200
Mm-hmm.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:05.520
"A Certain Scientific Accelerator"

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.760
"#05 DA (Security Officer Darkness)"

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.550
I promise we'll rescue you.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:27.810
"So then, jackpot!

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.190
Misaka pushed the can coffee button,
but then, as a reward for herself,

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.770
thought maybe she should go grab
a lumpy pomegranate cider, too,"

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.150
says Misaka Misaka,
with the tiniest bit of regret.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:43.660
"Aw, that lumpiness could
really becoming habit forming,"

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.740
says Misaka Misaka, thinking back
on how delicious the juice is,

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.040
and starting to become sad.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.210
"But on the other hand, we must be
thoughtful toward patients first, right"

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.710
says Misaka Misaka,
pushing back her own feelings,

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.710
and portraying herself as a can-do girl.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.720
"Jeez, you should let me take care of this,"

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.510
says Misaka Misaka, insisting.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.440
"I wish you'd turn to Misaka
to do the things you can't do,"

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.650
communicates Misaka Misaka to you.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:27.370
Damn it, I can't even make
her out clearly right now.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.940
We're running out of ammo!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.170
Fall back! We have to regroup!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:48.970
Forward!

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.230
I still don't understand it.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:02.150
How could DA have possibly come
from the same roots as Antiskill?

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.880
They may be the same roots,
but theirs have gone rotten.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:09.620
They're a group whose members
have received disciplinary action

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.010
for taking their
peacekeeping activities too far.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:16.870
But why did DA's sponsors
leave them hanging now?

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:23.460
Dogs that do not obey
the hunter are done away with.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.640
Branch 05 is engaging!
Our equipment is superior,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.890
but Antiskill has an endless
supply of reinforcements!

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.310
The way things are headed,
each branch will be neutralized by them!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.980
We have no intention of
waging all-out war with Antiskill.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.730
We're going to inflict
devastating damage on them,

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.280
and force them to the negotiating table.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.490
Hey, Dax! I know you're listening!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.080
What happened to that weapon that was
supposed to turn the tide of the battle?

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.330
What? If there is such a thing,
out with it, already!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.250
Esther got away from me,

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.580
and getting Last Order, who serves
as the core of it, was another fiasco.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.830
It's entirely because of your failures
that it got hung up. Mm-hmm.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.720
Isn't there any way to
use it in its present state?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.010
Well, you know. You guys are in luck.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:13.720
If I get my hands on one of the Sisters,
I think I can swing something, mm-hmm.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.270
Sisters?

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:20.480
What happened to that hostage you took?
She still hasn't arrived here.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.520
Oh, <i>that</i> hostage?

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:24.190
So if we turn her over to you,

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:27.490
your weapon that will turn
the tide is going to work?

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.410
Yeah, pretty much.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.950
The hostage just arrived at Branch 01.
Taking her to you.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.700
Dax, you get that weapon working.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.290
Yeah, I know.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.250
As if. Mm-hmm.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.460
I think it's about time I cut ties
to those justice-obsessed fools.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:48.420
At least, once I have the Sister,
then it's bye-bye.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:52.720
Mm-hmm. If I can't get my hands on her...

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.470
That'll do, right, Hirumi?

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:04.790
Hmm?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.510
You unruly mob! All you've got are numbers!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.550
Our theory of justice 
does not bend to numbers!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.510
What?! Are you actually 
telling me to carry this

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.850
to Chemistry Building 6 of Seiin High School
without any reinforcements?!

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:45.650
It's a vital component for
a weapon that will turn the tide?

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.030
All right.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.900
We're using the Tarantula.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:50.490
--Yes, sir.
--Yes, sir.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:58.240
They said a huge bag with
a girl inside is DA's ace in the hole.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.120
We'll have to nip that in the bud.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.460
Leader, where are we going?

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.670
The Sukunabikona Foods supplement factory.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.380
They've stopped fighting back.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.220
Are they out of ammunition?

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.350
Either way, we're not going
to get anywhere like this.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.850
We can't let them get out into the city.
We're moving in and hitting them again.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.730
What is that?

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.450
Heavy construction equipment?
No, it isn't. Stand ready!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.810
Fall back! Our shields
can't protect against that!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.010
What was that?!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:55.680
Fall back!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.790
They even have a monster like this?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.950
DA has a multi-legged weapon like that?!

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:08.670
Get reinforcements and some
antitank guns down there at once!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.210
It's turning its back to us again!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.340
The ass-mounted Gatling gun is firing!

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.720
Can't we do something
about that Gatling gun?!

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:24.640
Amazing. We may not even
have to rely on Hishigata.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:25.680
Don't get ahead of yourself.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.640
Our mission is to deliver 
this package safely.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.270
Nice moves.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.480
Ito!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.400
Up!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.370
Where are you headed, out-of-season Santa?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:50.830
Since I'm not dealing with children,
I can give this my all!

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:06.930
Tch!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:10.270
A person?!

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.020
You guys are inconceivable scum!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.420
Damn! The difference in
our firepower is too great!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.540
Where are those reinforcements?!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.920
So that's what these are supposed to be.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:37.630
Who are you?

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.340
What happened to my men?

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.840
They're all dead.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.140
Now we can finally get to the heart of this.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:55.610
Okay, let's get in after them quick
and finish the job!

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.820
--Yeah!
--Yeah!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:03.910
Tch.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:07.190
Then I'll just settle it all with <i>these</i>!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.060
Die!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.390
Die!

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.150
Die some more!

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:42.570
This is the fate of those who oppose DA!

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.700
This is hell...

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.050
Paper airplanes?

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:00.880
Someone's ability?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.340
Wh-What? What just happened?

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.890
String Juicers can even
slice through reinforced ceramic.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:16.150
What are those blasts?!

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.540
What exactly is going on?!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:46.260
Hey, do you read me? Hey!

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.550
Yeah.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.470
You have some weirdos in your path.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:52.970
These guys?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:16.410
Th-They're... Nakimoto's cleaners?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.000
They're going after their own people?

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.460
This is no time for a three-way battle!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.170
The Tarantula can only buy us 30 minutes.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:29.430
We need support, as per 
the original operation.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:30.640
Copy that.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:37.180
Dark-siders--the trash
that lurk about Academy City!

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.060
As long as I'm wrecking
stuff anyway, take this!

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.240
Die!

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.590
Impossible! They stopped me?!
Is that psychokinesis?!

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:10.040
Even if it is, the Tarantula weighs 120 tons!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:16.470
It isn't psychokinesis, you see.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.520
My ability is control
over frictional coefficients.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:22.650
So then, that business earlier was you?

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.810
Mm-hmm.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:30.030
Hey! Doesn't matter! If you can't go forward,
you can take another route!

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.030
G-Got it!

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.080
Ah, he's getting away!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.000
Is this one of those tactical retreat things?

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.580
If he gets away, we forfeit our contract.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.340
You're not getting away.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.890
I-I can't control it! Damn it!

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:03.060
If I increase the frictional coefficient
of the floor under one leg,

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.730
the other legs will just spin their wheels.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.350
What are <i>you</i> doing in there?!

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.740
Don't lose your head. You're almost there.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.850
I don't want to create any more...

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.640
...unhappiness.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:29.650
Adonai, are you all right?

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.370
Y-You saved me.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.510
Thank goodness.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:50.870
That's the huge bag with the girl
in it they mentioned over the radio...

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.630
...isn't it?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:56.090
You kept our spoils safe for us.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.800
Thanks for your help.

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.720
There might even be a bonus
available for packing her to go.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:05.180
Who are these people? They're a
different group than DA and Hishigata.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:08.400
If you leave the bag there and walk away,
we're willing to let you go.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:14.860
Disposing of you wasn't included in our job.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.990
We can be accommodating in that regard,
though it is kind of a dark area.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.240
And will such a "dark" organization

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.930
really keep its promises?!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:29.080
You?! We'll discuss this later.
Let a grown-up handle this.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:30.670
Who are you?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.090
If it means protecting her, I'm on your side.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.590
I'll take care of this.
You take her and get away from here!

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.760
That uniform--Antiskill.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.370
Oh, so you're a goody-goody.

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:47.020
Goody-goodies hide behind
the teacher and poke at us.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.770
Yeah, maybe we'd better
kill them, don't you think?

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.270
Okay, how about we do them
while we're getting the teacher?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.480
--Agreed!
--Agreed!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.400
--Me! Me! I'll do it! I'll do it! Me! Me! Me!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:57.530
--Oh, okay.
--Me! Me! I'll do it! I'll do it! Me! Me! Me!

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.320
--Do you need any help?
--Me! Me! I'll do it! I'll do it! Me! Me! Me!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.120
No thank you, of course!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.200
What is the deal with those girls?

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.200
I don't need any help
to take out a single teacher.

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:30.310
Ta-da!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:45.950
"There, charge complete!"
says Misaka Misaka, helping you out.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:55.420
"Okay, if you need anything else,
don't hesitate to holler,"

00:19:55.420 --> 00:20:00.420
whispers Misaka Misaka to you. See you later!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:06.850
Damn this busted-up brain.
If not for the Misaka Network's help,

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.680
I couldn't even form a complete sentence.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.690
"The civilian...

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:15.770
...is No. 10046," says Misaka,

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:19.530
disclosing the information she
declines to share with Last Order.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:40.410
"Huh?! Where are you going?!"
asks Misaka Misaka, having a bad feeling.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.260
Well? Well?

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.180
Well?

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.350
The convenience store!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:52.690
Yay! Misaka can't get the idea of lumpy
pomegranate cider out of her head!

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:55.690
Mm, on the other hand,
thinking about this for a minute...

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.470
Lumpy?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.900
Yes, lumpy!

00:21:00.570 --> 00:21:02.120
Lumpy...

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.410
Mm-hmm, lumpy!

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:06.030
Lum...

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.450
...py!

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.660
"And it's the lumpiness of pomegranates,"

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.200
expresses Misaka Misaka to you.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:22.340
Huh? Misaka Misaka is taking
a suspicious view of your actions.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:26.590
Tch, you really think I'm going
to come across any pomegranates?

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.450
Damn it, I'm getting it from all sides.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:50.040
But then, it's just what
I need to help with my rehab.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:36.960
"Next time"

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:41.530
"Scavenger"
